      "writtenOn": "2023-01-06T15:26:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This raises an interesting question: is having an empty ramdisk equivalent to not having one at all in every aspect ... Why not keep the `Option` in `Payload::initrd`? That would match our future verification cases:\n\n- `None` and have a ramdisk hash descriptor: failed\n- `None` and don\u0027t have a ramdisk hash descriptor: passed\n- `Some` and have a ramdisk hash descriptor: verify it\n- `Some` and don\u0027t have a ramdisk hash descriptor: ??? (failed, I guess)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 401,
        "startChar": 55,
        "endLine": 401,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "734a93c72788de6ec36f161b55ba096a239b6ad6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4173024a_deadb685",
        "filename": "pvmfw/avb/src/verify.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 401,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-09T13:22:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e having an empty ramdisk equivalent to not having one at all in every aspect\n\nIt\u0027s not exactly the same. If we try to read the partition `initrd` when it is empty, an error will be raised in `read_from_partition`. \n\n\u003e Why not keep the Option in Payload::initrd ?\n\nActually I\u0027d like `Payload::verify_partition()` just to be a pvmfw customized wrapper around `avb_slot_verify` without conditional branches. The method is already pretty long like this. Then then `verify_payload` will handle the logic the logic around whether payload has initrd or not.\n\n- If `initrd` is None, then call `Payload::verify_partition([kernel])` and check the kernel footer has only one hash descriptor with `avb_descriptor_get_all`.\n- If `initrd` is Some, then call `Payload::verify_partition([kernel, initrd_normal, initrd_debug])` and check the result to decide the mode. (Maybe also assert that kernel footer has only three hash descriptors?)",
      "parentUuid": "c4bab266_c2e3c1d5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 401,
        "startChar": 55,
        "endLine": 401,
